B = [
('Lanvin','Europe','1920s-30s','fashion','In the style of Lanvin, soft, graceful, romantic femininity with a jeweled couture touch. Full bell-shaped volumes sit over a fitted dropped waist, finished with bows, ribbons and gently gathered trims. Fine silk surfaces are richly worked with intricate beading and embroidery, with small flower appliques scattered lightly. Palette is powder blue, rose pink, lilac, silver and cream in delicate tonal harmony. Any emblem is a simple stylised line drawing inside a round frame in cream and blue. Tender, polished, sparkling and gently nostalgic, with early twentieth century elegance.'),
('Schiaparelli','Europe','1930s','fashion','In the style of Schiaparelli, witty surrealist couture where ordinary things become clever visual jokes. Illusion tricks make knitted, printed or embroidered details pretend to be something else, and familiar objects are reimagined as sculptural forms. Shocking hot pink is the signature colour, set against black, gold and deep jewel tones. Silhouettes have strong padded shoulders and sharp exaggerated structure, with bold exposed fasteners and ornaments modelled as body parts, creatures or glass flowers, plus dense gold embroidery. Daring, artistic, humorous and sculptural, with 1930s avant-garde glamour.'),
('Fendi','Europe','1960s-present','fashion','In the style of Fendi, Roman luxury with plush, playful, craft-heavy richness. A repeating double-letter monogram pattern in brown on tan is a core surface idea, alongside patchwork and inlaid fur or leather worked like fine marquetry. Fluffy trims are dyed in bright candy colours, and whimsical little charms with cartoon eyes add humour. Tailoring is sleek and clean in camel, black and white, with compact shapes carried close to the body and secured by neat magnetic or metal clasps. Warm, tactile, witty and indulgent.'),
('Bottega Veneta','Europe','1970s-present','leather goods','In the style of Bottega Veneta, quiet luxury built on woven leather made of soft strips interlaced in a tight, even basketweave grid, applied as the surface of any object. Strips are thick and wide, supple and slightly slouchy, with minimal hardware and no external logos. Palette is butter yellow, parakeet green, burnt orange, taupe, chocolate and black, rich but never loud. A single discreet gold knot may serve as a closure or accent. Understated, tactile, soft to the touch, with quiet craftsmanship as the only signature.'),
('Mulberry','Europe','1970s-present','leather goods','In the style of Mulberry, British country-house heritage in rugged yet polished leather. Glossy or naturally grained hide in oak brown, chocolate, oxblood and navy is shaped into sturdy, practical forms with flap closures, long straps and a front lock in solid brass. Brass studs and fittings are used sparingly, with contrast stitching and a small tree emblem embossed in gold. Surfaces are meant to age and soften with use. Traditional, durable, countryside, confident and quietly rich.'),
('Swatch','Europe','1980s-90s','accessories','In the style of Swatch, playful, loud, pop-art design in light, thin, flat moulded plastic with a jelly-like gloss. Translucent and skeleton-like cases reveal the workings inside. Surfaces carry bold graphic patterns, stripes, dots, squiggles and artist-style prints in neon and pastel colours. Wide soft bands loop closed, markings and numerals are tiny and printed, and hands are chunky in bright red, yellow or blue. Colours clash on purpose. Cheerful, cheap-chic, collectable and irreverent, with an unmistakable 1980s postmodern pop attitude.'),
('Issey Miyake','East Asia','1980s-present','fashion','In the style of Issey Miyake, sculptural garments in permanently heat-pressed micro-pleated polyester that springs back into shape, cut as oversized geometric volumes such as tubes, rectangles, circles and folded origami-like forms. Silhouettes are loose, weightless and body-skimming rather than fitted, with exaggerated sleeves and cocoon shapes. Fabrics have corrugated vertical or zigzag pleats that catch light in ripples, plus crinkled, bonded and sheer technical textiles. Colour is either muted charcoal, black, ivory and indigo or sudden saturated blocks of orange, fuchsia, cobalt, lime and yellow, sometimes in rainbow stripes or bold painted graphics. Minimal seams, no visible fastenings, sporty comfort, quiet architectural calm and bright airy gallery lighting.'),
('Comme des Garcons','East Asia','1980s-present','fashion','In the style of Comme des Garcons, deconstructed avant-garde design with asymmetric, deliberately distorted silhouettes, bulbous padded humps, oversized stiff shapes, exposed raw seams, unfinished frayed hems, holes, inside-out construction and layered mismatched panels. Dominant colour is severe black, then stark white, grey and a single shock of red, with occasional gingham, polka dot, tartan or flat pop prints. Materials are felt, crumpled cotton, boiled and distressed knits, lace, patent and cheap-looking synthetics treated as luxury. Shapes ignore the body, parts are too long or placed in the wrong spot, and forms hang like sculptures. A small simple heart with two eyes works as a playful mark. Stark white spaces, austere, intellectual and rebellious.'),
('Yohji Yamamoto','East Asia','1980s-present','fashion','In the style of Yohji Yamamoto, voluminous draped black design cut in oversized, asymmetric layers that hang away from the body so the silhouette becomes a dark shadowy cloud. Materials are matte wool gabardine, crinkled cotton, heavy linen, felted wool and fluid jersey, with raw edges, big collars, tilted lapels, trailing hems and long scarf-like panels. Palette is overwhelmingly black, then charcoal, deep navy, off-white and rare blood red. Tailoring is slouchy, androgynous and undone, with flat understated accessories and occasional large calligraphic or graphic prints in white on black. Poetic, melancholic, monastic, dim moody lighting, wabi-sabi imperfection.'),
('Kenzo','East Asia','1970s-80s','fashion','In the style of Kenzo, joyful, bright, folkloric design that mixes wide kimono-like sleeves, loose smock shapes, patchwork, quilting and layered ethnic prints in a single look. Large flowers, stripes, ginghams, checks and paisley are combined at clashing scale in saturated tomato red, yellow, turquoise, emerald, pink and purple. Fabrics are cotton, soft jersey, knits and light gauzy weaves, cut in a relaxed, unstructured, unisex way with drawstring waists and bold stripes, and big knitted pieces carry jungle animal motifs. A cheerful, colourful, exotic jungle-and-garden fantasy, sunlit, slightly naive, with a fluffy hand-painted look.'),
('Uniqlo','East Asia','2000s-present','fashion','In the style of Uniqlo, clean, democratic, everyday basics in a restrained, uniform range. Simple regular-fit shapes, neither tight nor oversized, in smooth matte fabric with flat tidy stitching, light insulated quilting in neat horizontal channels, fine soft knits and plain crisp weaves. No visible logos, at most a tiny red square. Colours are a tidy wall of solid shades such as white, black, navy, grey, olive, camel, burgundy, mustard and pastel blue, shown in perfectly aligned stacks on bright white shelves. Plain sans-serif labels in red and white, bright even retail lighting and white backgrounds. Neutral, functional and orderly.'),
('Muji','East Asia','1980s-present','homeware','In the style of Muji, plain, unbranded, no-logo design in a quiet, anonymous aesthetic. Natural, undyed materials such as unbleached cotton, linen, paper, recycled cardboard, raw pale wood, rubber, brushed aluminium and clear frosted plastic keep their honest look. Colours stay in beige, oatmeal, off-white, light grey, charcoal, navy and muted black, with matte uncoloured finishes. Forms are minimal and rounded-rectangular, with soft edges, a single function and no decoration. Tiny simple sans-serif labels in black sit on kraft brown paper or white card, and objects are arranged in neat grids. Calm, empty, modest and serene, with soft daylight and generous empty space.'),
('Onitsuka Tiger','East Asia','1960s-present','footwear','In the style of Onitsuka Tiger, slim, retro, low-profile sporting design from the 1960s and 70s. Elongated narrow shapes with flat thin rubber soles and a contrasting side stripe formed by crossing wavy parallel lines. Bodies are cream or white with accents in red, navy, yellow, forest green and black, often two-tone suede and breathable mesh panels with tonal reinforced parts. Small details include tiny perforations, pale gum-coloured edging, thin laces, a small gold stamped label and a tiny embroidered striding big cat mark. Clean, nostalgic, compact and athletic, with a subtle vintage gym mood.'),
('Mikimoto','East Asia','1900s-present','jewellery','In the style of Mikimoto, classic jewellery centred on round, lustrous cultured pearls with a creamy white to pale pink glow and a mirror-like surface, strung in long, uniform, graduated strands, ropes and multiple rows with a small clasp. Settings are restrained and elegant in polished white and yellow gold and platinum, with small round diamonds used as pave or tiny accent rims. Designs feel graceful, symmetrical and timeless, sometimes with soft rounded shapes inspired by shells, waves and flowers. Presented on dark navy velvet or in pale blue boxes. Calm, refined and luminous, soft diffused lighting.'),
('Hosoo','East Asia','traditional-present','textiles','In the style of Hosoo, richly woven silk brocade with metallic gold and silver foil threads, fine glossy surfaces, dense jacquard patterns and a subtle changing sheen. Patterns include geometric lattices, waves, clouds, flowers, bark textures and abstract digital-like lines in very fine repeat. Colours are deep ink black, vermilion red, indigo, ivory, aged gold, silver and soft muted purple, with tiny metallic sparkle. The cloth is stiff, flat and ornate, suited to architectural surfaces as well as dress, and the weave shows a thin layered gleam where metallic strips meet silk. Traditional and contemporary at once, luxurious, patient and handcrafted, in soft side light that makes the metallic threads glow.'),
('A Bathing Ape','East Asia','1990s-2000s','fashion','In the style of A Bathing Ape, loud, cartoonish, hype-driven streetwear. Giant graphic mouths with white teeth and blue eyes run boldly across the whole front of a garment, and a simple cartoon head in profile serves as the logo. Camouflage appears in bright unexpected colours such as pink, purple, green, yellow and blue, with multi-colour gradients, stacked rainbow stripes, bold white text and glow-in-the-dark prints. Star-shaped glossy patent panels add shine. Fit is oversized and boxy in heavy cotton and fleece. Playful, colourful, hip-hop inspired Tokyo street mood.'),
('Evisu','East Asia','1990s-2000s','fashion','In the style of Evisu, premium Japanese selvedge raw denim in deep indigo, heavy, stiff and rugged, with a red selvedge line on the outer seam. A large painted white logo of two sweeping curves, like a stylised bird, is applied as a bold hand-painted mark. High-contrast orange and gold thread stitching, copper rivets, a leather patch, a straight narrow leg and a slightly high rise define the cut. Wear develops as sharp honeycomb creases and whisker fades. Embossed metal buttons and hand-painted curved lines add detail. Rugged, vintage, heritage workwear mood.'),
('Shiatzy Chen','East Asia','1990s-present','fashion','In the style of Shiatzy Chen, elegant East meets West design that blends tailored modern cuts with Chinese tradition. Standing mandarin collars, frog knot closures and asymmetric side fastenings sit on slim, refined, graceful shapes. Fabrics are silk satin, brocade, jacquard, embroidered tulle and wool crepe, with embroidered or woven motifs of peonies, bamboo, cranes, clouds and calligraphy brush strokes. Palette favours jade green, imperial red, ink black, ivory, deep blue and gold thread, with delicate piping, braided trim and tassel details. A poised, quiet-luxury, nostalgic old Shanghai mood in soft studio light.'),
('Shanghai Tang','East Asia','1990s-2000s','fashion','In the style of Shanghai Tang, a glossy modern take on Chinese imperial and 1930s Shanghai dress, with form-fitting lines, mandarin collars, cloth knot fastenings, side slits and piped edges. Colours are intense and playful, such as imperial yellow, lacquer red, fuchsia, jade green, turquoise, orange and purple, in a candy-bright palette alongside black and gold. Satin, brocade, jacquard and embroidered silk carry dragons, peonies, double happiness symbols, bats, clouds and lotus flowers, with padded quilting. Lacquered red surfaces, tassels and enamel inlays add richness. Cheerful, nostalgic, theatrical Hong Kong glamour.'),
('Sabyasachi','South Asia','2000s-present','fashion','In the style of Sabyasachi, opulent, romantic Indian heirloom richness with a vintage, slightly distressed and layered look. Deep earthy jewel colours such as rich red, burnt orange, marigold, mustard, moss green, teal and faded rose cover the surface. Heavy hand embroidery in dense gold metallic thread, silk thread, sequins, mirror work and tassels combines with block-printed florals and tiger or paisley motifs on silk, velvet, organza and tulle. Sheer veils have scalloped borders. Jewellery is chunky antique gold with uncut stones, big gems and pearl ropes, layered thickly. Regal, heritage mood, warm golden light and a faded-palace feel.'),
('Fabindia','South Asia','1960s-present','fashion','In the style of Fabindia, handloom and hand-block-printed cotton design with a rural craftsman feel. Relaxed, straight, loose shapes in soft textured cotton and silk-cotton blends show visible slub in the weave. Colours are earthy natural dyes such as indigo, madder red, turmeric yellow, rust, ochre, olive, charcoal and undyed cream. Patterns are small repeating floral and geometric block prints, ikat, dotted tie-dye, stripes and checks, with slightly irregular hand-printed edges. Stitching is simple, with wooden buttons. Unfussy, honest, sun-washed and warm, as if hung on rustic wooden shelves.'),
('Manish Malhotra','South Asia','1990s-present','fashion','In the style of Manish Malhotra, glamorous Bollywood-style couture, lavishly embellished and sensual. Sheer net, tulle, georgette and silk are covered with sparkling sequins, crystals, beads, pearls and gold or silver thread embroidery across fitted bodices, borders and trailing capes. Palette includes champagne, blush pink, ivory, emerald, wine red, midnight blue, black and metallic gold. Silhouettes are body-hugging with plunging necklines, corset-like structure, structured sleeves and dramatic flared skirts with long trains. Ornate gold accessories complete the look. Glossy, red-carpet mood, high-contrast studio lighting and shimmering texture.'),
('Tanishq','South Asia','1990s-present','jewellery','In the style of Tanishq, rich, symmetrical, festive jewellery in warm 22 carat yellow gold, with heavy layered forms, stacks of bangles and hanging bell-like drops. Motifs include lotus flowers, peacocks, paisley mango shapes, leaves, elephants, filigree and temple-like architecture. Surfaces combine polished gold with fine granulation, rows of uncut diamonds, rubies, emeralds, pearls and coloured enamel, with delicate hanging pearl drops. Displayed on red velvet and lit by warm golden light. A lighter side uses minimalist single stones and fine rose gold lines for everyday wear.'),
('Raymond','South Asia','1920s-present','fashion','In the style of Raymond, classic worsted wool suiting and tailored menswear, formal, sober and gentlemanly. Smooth fine-twill cloth in navy, charcoal, black, grey and tan carries subtle pinstripes, herringbone, glen checks and windowpane patterns. The silhouette is perfectly cut with structured shoulders, notch lapels, a nipped waist and a sharp crease, worn with crisp white shirt, silk tie and pocket square. Fabric is shown folded in neat stacks and swatch books. Dignified, traditional and aspirational, recalling mid-twentieth century wedding and office tailoring, with warm wood panelling and polished brass.'),
('Anokhi','South Asia','1970s-present','textiles','In the style of Anokhi, hand-block-printed cotton with fine repeating floral sprigs, vines, small buta motifs, lattice screens, paisleys and stripes printed in natural-looking dyes on soft white or cream voile. Colours are indigo, madder red, saffron, sage green, mustard, rose pink and charcoal, in two or three tones per print with slightly offset, hand-stamped edges. Shapes are loose and simple, with bound seams, quilting and small tassels. Fresh, breezy, Rajasthani-craft mood, shown on sunlit whitewashed walls with piles of folded block-printed cloth.'),
('Shrujan','South Asia','traditional-present','textiles','In the style of Shrujan, densely hand-stitched embroidery in bright thread on dark or plain ground, with tiny mirrors sewn in using chain stitch, herringbone and buttonhole borders. Motifs are repeating peacocks, parrots, flowers, mango shapes, geometric diamonds, stars and tiny mandala medallions arranged in tight bands and symmetrical grids. Colours are vivid magenta, scarlet, turquoise, canary yellow, green and white against black, indigo or deep red. Highly textured, glittering, tactile surfaces of shimmering mirrors and tight thread, with folk-craft joyfulness.'),
('Kala Raksha','South Asia','traditional-present','textiles','In the style of Kala Raksha, artisan-made embroidery, applique and patchwork on handwoven cotton. Precisely counted triangular geometry is stitched in satin stitch, forming tiny diamonds, zig-zags and stars in mirror-like symmetry. Colours are bold contrasts of magenta, orange, yellow, green, royal blue and white on black or deep indigo cloth, with quilted patchwork in reds and blacks. Small mirrors are set at the centre of motifs. Meticulous, handmade, vibrant, desert-village craft mood.'),
('Nalli Silks','South Asia','traditional-present','textiles','In the style of Nalli Silks, heavy hand-woven pure silk with rich lustre, a broad contrasting border, a separate decorated end panel and woven gold or silver thread motifs. Motifs include temple towers, checks, peacocks, parrots, elephants, mango paisley, lotus flowers and fine vertical stripes. Colours are vivid and deep, such as peacock blue, magenta, parrot green, mustard, maroon, saffron and black with gold, with border colours contrasting sharply against the body. The cloth is thick, stiff, glossy and falls in heavy pleats, shown folded in stacks on white sheets in bright light.'),
('Barefoot Colombo','South Asia','1960s-present','textiles','In the style of Barefoot Colombo, handloom cotton with striped and checked weaves in bold bands of saturated colour such as coral, turquoise, lime green, mustard, indigo, magenta and white. Plain-weave and slubby handwoven cloth shows visible warp threads, tasselled fringes and playful geometric stripes. Occasional hand-painted or batik motifs of flowers and leaves appear. Relaxed, tropical, cheerful mood, shown in sunlit verandas with palm leaves and rattan, with a handmade, unpolished texture.'),
('Jim Thompson','Southeast Asia','1950s-present','textiles','In the style of Jim Thompson, hand-woven silk with a lustrous, slightly slubby shimmer. Fabrics show iridescent two-tone shot effects in jewel colours such as sapphire, emerald, ruby, saffron, fuchsia, plum and turquoise, plus rich plains. Prints show stylised animals, tropical leaves, orchids, lotus, bamboo, pagoda motifs and bold stripes, drawn in a flat painterly style with generous colour fields. Cloth is displayed rolled in rainbow stacks. Warm, exotic, elegant mood with teak wood and soft tropical light.'),
('Batik Keris','Southeast Asia','1970s-present','textiles','In the style of Batik Keris, wax-resist dyed cotton and silk in dense repeating patterns of parang diagonal waves, overlapping circles, cloud swirls, floral sprays, birds and trailing vines. Typical colours are warm sogan brown, deep indigo, dark black, cream and golden yellow, plus brighter coastal tones in red, turquoise and green. Fine crackle lines show where the wax cracked, and slight irregularities reveal the hand-drawn pen or copper stamp. Formal, refined, ceremonial Javanese mood, shown draped on bamboo racks.'),
('Danar Hadi','Southeast Asia','1960s-present','textiles','In the style of Danar Hadi, royal-court batik, hand-drawn and stamped on cotton and silk in elaborate classical patterns, with diagonal blade-like bands, circle grids, star flowers and lotus motifs filling the cloth evenly in fine linework. Colours are dignified earth tones of sogan brown, midnight indigo, cream white and soft black, with occasional touches of gold paint. Surfaces are hand-finished with a slightly crackled wax texture. Dignified, traditional, courtly mood, shown in dim museum-like light.'),
('Vakko','Middle East','1960s-present','fashion','In the style of Vakko, large square twill silk printed with detailed painterly scenes, tile patterns, tulips, carnations, flower patterns, arabesques, waterside views and maritime and horse motifs, finished with hand-rolled hems. Colours are saturated cobalt, turquoise, coral red, emerald, gold and ivory, in dense multi-colour compositions bordered by a decorative frame. Tailoring is polished, with furs, silk blouses, boxy jackets and long coats. Elegant, cosmopolitan, orientalist-meets-modern mood, with rich satin sheen and gold chain edges.'),
('Elie Saab','Middle East','2000s-present','fashion','In the style of Elie Saab, romantic, feminine red-carpet couture, with long sheer columns and full skirts over fitted bodices, plunging necklines, illusion lace, delicate floral applique and beading in gold, silver and crystal. Fabrics are tulle, chiffon, Chantilly lace, silk crepe and satin, in soft powder pink, blush, ivory, champagne, lilac, sky blue, emerald and rich red. Details include embroidered lace sleeves, sweeping trains, scattered flower petals, cinched waists and sparkling bodices that fade into transparent skirts. Dreamy, luxurious, fairytale mood, in soft glowing light.'),
('Bonwire Kente Weavers','Africa','traditional-present','textiles','In the style of Bonwire Kente Weavers, hand-loomed narrow strips of silk and cotton, about four inches wide, sewn edge to edge into large cloths. Brilliant geometric patterns of interlocking bands, squares, zigzags, stepped diamonds and blocks in gold, kente yellow, deep red, emerald green, royal blue, black and white. Weft-faced areas alternate with striped plain sections, and supplementary thread motifs create tiny symbols such as ladders and checks. Surfaces are rich, thick, slightly ridged and rhythmic, each strip a different arrangement. Regal, ceremonial, celebratory mood.'),
('Studio 189','Africa','2010s-present','fashion','In the style of Studio 189, ethical, handmade design centred on hand-dyed indigo, hand-batiked cloth, resist patterns, hand-woven fabrics and block-printed wax prints. Shapes are relaxed and modern, with wide legs, boxy tops, flowing wraps and kimono-like layers in cotton and linen. Palette includes deep indigo blue, white, earthy ochre, rust, black and bright accent colours such as orange and green, in tie-dye swirls, hand-drawn stripes, dots, geometric grids and flowing batik lines. Visible hand-dyed unevenness and crisp artisanal texture. Breezy, warm, socially conscious, sunlit West African mood.'),
('Maxhosa Africa','Africa','2010s-present','fashion','In the style of Maxhosa Africa, bold beadwork patterns turned into jacquard knit, with sharp geometric bands of triangles, diamonds, chevrons, zigzags, stepped blocks and horizontal stripes. Colours are vibrant and contrasting, such as red, orange, mustard, cobalt blue, emerald, turquoise, pink and black against cream or deep neutral grounds, in rich saturated blocks. Materials are chunky mohair, merino wool and soft cotton. Patterns repeat symmetrically like beaded collars. Warm, proud, celebratory, heritage-meets-contemporary mood.'),
('Lisa Folawiyo','Africa','2010s-present','fashion','In the style of Lisa Folawiyo, bold wax print cotton combined with heavy hand-embellishment, using beads, sequins, crystals, pearls, metallic thread and shell-like details sewn in dense clusters across bodices, collars, sleeves and hems. Silhouettes are modern and sculptural, with cropped shapes, peplum waists, structured shoulders, ruffled trumpet flares, fitted lines and playful cut-outs. Prints are bold and graphic in electric blue, tangerine, fuchsia, yellow, emerald and black and white, with embroidery that highlights the pattern outlines. Glamorous, festive, Afro-modern mood, glossy with sparkle and contrasting textures.'),
('Vlisco','Africa','1960s-present','textiles','In the style of Vlisco, wax-print cotton cloth with enormous vividly coloured designs printed identically on both sides with resin, leaving fine crackle veins where dye seeped through the wax. Motifs are oversized flowers, fruit, birds, feathers, fish, eyes, circles, hands, fans, scrolling vines and bold geometric patterns, outlined and shaded like block-print drawings. Palette is saturated and clashing such as cobalt and orange, scarlet and green, yellow and violet, turquoise and pink, black and white. Exuberant, expressive, festive market-stall mood.'),
('Thebe Magugu','Africa','2010s-present','fashion','In the style of Thebe Magugu, contemporary design that combines sharp tailoring with storytelling prints, with structured lines, pleats, crisp shirting and strong shoulders. Fabrics include wool, silk, crisp cotton and leather, with printed illustrations of portraits, plants, historical imagery and map-like graphics. Palette moves between deep forest green, burgundy, cobalt blue, mustard, cream, black and pastel pink, with precise seams, contrasting piping and nipped waists. Playful and intellectual, polished, artful and modern, in clean gallery light.'),
('Havaianas','Latin America','1960s-present','footwear','In the style of Havaianas, thin, flat, lightweight rubber forms with a glossy matte finish and a slightly squishy feel. The surface is textured with a rice-grain pattern of tiny raised ridges, and straps are flat wide bands in a Y shape. Colours are juicy, summery solids such as white, yellow, lime green, hot pink, turquoise, red, navy and orange, with a contrasting colour for the strap against the base and flag-like stripes. Two-tone, simple and cheerful, shown against beach sand, blue sea and bright sun. Casual and tropical mood.'),
('Osklen','Latin America','1990s-present','fashion','In the style of Osklen, relaxed Rio luxury sportswear, lightweight and technical, in natural and eco-friendly materials such as organic cotton, linen, wool, recycled fibres and exotic fish leather. Palette is sand, off-white, navy, olive, grey, terracotta, deep teal and ocean blue with pops of orange. Prints show waves, sea creatures, forest leaves and Amazon-inspired graphics, with sleek minimal pockets and zippers. Nature-loving, outdoorsy, sun-washed beach-to-city mood with soft golden light and mountain backdrops.'),
('Farm Rio','Latin America','2010s-present','fashion','In the style of Farm Rio, exuberant Brazilian tropical design with flowing, airy shapes in viscose, cotton and chiffon. Prints are lush and hand-painted, with giant flowers, banana leaves, toucans, macaws, jaguars, monkeys, butterflies, fruit and palm trees, plus stripes, in saturated pink, red, orange, yellow, emerald, turquoise and royal blue. Details include puff sleeves, tiered ruffles, smocking, tie straps, embroidered trim and bright pom-pom accents. Carefree, joyful, vacation mood, shown against jungle foliage and bright blue sky.'),
('H.Stern','Latin America','1960s-present','jewellery','In the style of H.Stern, fine jewellery that showcases large coloured gemstones such as emerald, aquamarine, tourmaline, topaz, amethyst and citrine in smooth cabochon and faceted cuts, set in polished yellow and rose gold. Shapes are organic and sculptural, with flowing curves, wave and leaf forms and bold chunky volumes. Designs often combine textured gold with a single huge gem or bright candy-coloured stones stacked in bands, with smooth rounded forms that feel modern and tropical. Colours are saturated greens, blues, purples and warm golden yellow. Confident, glamorous and sunny, against dark velvet with bright spotlights.'),
('Melissa','Latin America','1980s-present','footwear','In the style of Melissa, glossy jelly-like plastic moulded in one piece with sculptural bows, flowers, buckles and cutouts. The surface is shiny, translucent or glittery with a faint sweet-candy look. Colours are jelly pink, lilac, mint, clear transparent, baby blue, yellow, red, black and metallic glitter. Shapes are playful and rounded, with chunky soles, bubble-like toes, ribbed textures and puffy edges. Fun, youthful, pop-art toy mood, shown on pastel studio backdrops with glossy reflections.'),
('Pineda Covalin','Latin America','2000s-present','fashion','In the style of Pineda Covalin, intricate, richly coloured silk prints drawn from pre-Hispanic and folk culture, such as sun-disc calendars, jaguars, eagles, serpents, agave, skulls, floral crowns, hummingbirds, corn, cacti, tile patterns and embroidery. Prints are dense and symmetrical, framed by decorative borders, in bold turquoise, cochineal red, marigold orange, jade green, magenta, cobalt and gold on silk twill. Hand-rolled hems and bright packaging. Festive, ornate, folk-art mood with warm, saturated colour.'),
('R.M. Williams','Oceania','1930s-present','footwear','In the style of R.M. Williams, rugged, practical outback leatherwork, sleek and refined, made from a single piece of leather wrapped and stitched with minimal seams, in chestnut brown, tan, black and oxblood. Details include a pull tab, elastic side gussets, a slightly pointed rounded toe, a stacked leather heel, a visible stitched welt and a smooth polished finish. Workwear touches use moleskin, oilskin, check cotton and wide leather belts in earth tones of khaki, sand, olive, navy and rust. Bush mood with red desert dust and golden light.'),
('Zimmermann','Oceania','2000s-present','fashion','In the style of Zimmermann, romantic holiday design with floaty, feminine shapes, broderie anglaise, delicate lace, ruffles, puffed sleeves, tiered skirts, smocking, scalloped hems and tie-front details in linen, cotton, silk and chiffon. Prints are painterly florals, watercolour blooms, paisley, ditsy flowers, polka dots, stripes and bohemian tile motifs in cream, ivory, blush pink, sage green, butter yellow, cornflower blue, rich red and black. Cut-outs and frills appear in matching prints. Dreamy, sunny, coastal, bohemian mood, among wildflowers and white-washed beach houses.'),
('Akubra','Oceania','1870s-present','hats','In the style of Akubra, soft rabbit fur felt with a wide flat or slightly drooping brim, a tall crown with a centre dent and two pinched side dents, and a plain leather or ribbon band with a bound edge. Colours are fawn, tan, cream, grey, olive, brown and black, with a pale ribbon band. The surface is soft, slightly fuzzy, matte and suede-like, with sweat marks and creases developing with wear. Practical, rugged, sun-baked countryside mood, against red earth, eucalyptus and wide skies.'),
('Blundstone','Oceania','1870s-present','footwear','In the style of Blundstone, plain, hard-wearing, no-frills pull-on design with a rounded toe, elastic sides, black pull tabs and a smooth or waxed leather upper in brown, black or rustic tan. The sole is a thick chunky lugged tread in black with a contrasting pale or tan midsole stripe and visible stitching. The surface has a slightly scuffed utilitarian look, with a small label on the pull tab. Shown with muddy tracks, farmland and cool misty light. Honest, timeless work mood.'),
('Icebreaker','Oceania','1990s-present','fashion','In the style of Icebreaker, close-fitting fine soft merino knit, smooth, matte and slightly fuzzy, with flat seams and mountain-inspired minimalism. Colours are muted forest green, charcoal, deep navy, heather grey, rust, moss, stone and pale blue with occasional bright orange. Graphic touches include small sheep-like or mountain-line prints, subtle stripes and tiny sewn labels. Simple, natural, adventure-ready mood, shown in snowy alpine and misty hill landscapes.'),
('Paspaley','Oceania','1930s-present','jewellery','In the style of Paspaley, large, round, luminous white and golden pearls with a deep satiny lustre, strung as thick single strands, graduated lengths and long ropes, and set as earrings, rings and pendants. Metalwork is simple and smooth in white gold, yellow gold and platinum, sometimes with small clusters of diamonds. Shapes include baroque drops, wave-like clasps, shell and sea-inspired forms. Pearl colours range from cool silvery white to champagne and deep gold. Calm, ocean-luxury mood, on dark stone or white sand with soft aquamarine light.'),
('Dinosaur Designs','Oceania','1980s-present','jewellery','In the style of Dinosaur Designs, hand-poured resin in organic, sculptural, brightly coloured shapes. Forms are blobs, pebbles, waves and smooth curvy tubes in swirling marbled resin, with glossy, translucent surfaces mixing candy colours such as watermelon pink, tangerine, turquoise, lime, lilac, cobalt, ivory and deep black. Everything follows the same fluid, tactile forms with uneven hand-poured edges. Playful, artistic, joyful mood, on pastel backgrounds with colourful reflections.'),
('Country Road','Oceania','1970s-present','fashion','In the style of Country Road, relaxed smart-casual design with clean classic shapes, such as breton stripes and tailored easy lines. Palette is natural and understated, with white, navy, sand, oatmeal, olive, khaki, soft grey, terracotta and occasional sky blue. Fabrics are cotton, linen, wool and denim, and details are minimal with natural wooden buttons and neat stitching. Coastal neutral tones carry through to the home. Fresh, easy, sun-bleached beach house mood, in bright airy interiors.'),
('Swanndri','Oceania','1910s-present','fashion','In the style of Swanndri, heavy felted wool cloth in bold large checks and plaids, such as red and black, blue and black, green and black, mustard and navy. The cut is boxy and long, with a half-button or zip front, an attached hood, big patch pockets, a drawstring waist and reinforced elbows. The surface is dense, slightly fuzzy and water-resistant, with sturdy stitching and metal eyelets. Rugged farm and hunting mood, shown in misty green hills, sheep country and muddy tracks.'),
('Rip Curl','Oceania','1960s-present','fashion','In the style of Rip Curl, Australian surf culture, with black neoprene trimmed in bright coloured panels, bold stripes and flashes of red, yellow, aqua or lime. Large tropical or abstract graphics, drawstring waists and a curling wave swirl logo printed on chest and thigh. Palette is ocean blues, black, white, coral, sunshine yellow, teal and orange with faded vintage surf tones. Rugged and sporty. Sun-faded, salty, energetic beach mood, shown against breaking waves and sandy shores.'),
('Akris','Europe','1990s-present','fashion','In the style of Akris, Swiss quiet-luxury built on architectural minimalism, with precisely cut, straight, clean lines in double-faced wool, gabardine, silk crepe and crisp cotton. Palette is restrained, with black, ivory, camel, charcoal, navy, sand and soft grey, with occasional accents of coral or deep green. Details are subtle, such as laser-cut edges, flat welt seams, bonded hems, hidden closures and geometric architectural prints inspired by buildings. Silhouettes are clean, sharp and balanced, with a refined, understated, polished mood and cool gallery-like light.'),
('Jingdezhen Imperial Kilns','East Asia','Ming-Qing dynasties','ceramics','In the style of Jingdezhen Imperial Kilns, thin-walled white porcelain with a glassy, faintly bluish transparent glaze, painted under the glaze in rich cobalt blue. Motifs include coiling lotus scrolls, dragons chasing flaming pearls, fish and water weed, peony sprays and bands of cloud and wave forms, repeated in tight concentric bands. Cobalt shades range from pale silvery blue to deep inky blue with dark pooled spots. Forms are elegant and balanced, with rounded shoulders, narrow foot rings and crisp rims. Overglaze enamel variants add coral red, apple green, yellow and turquoise outlined in fine black.'),
('Longquan Celadon Kilns','East Asia','Song dynasty','ceramics','In the style of Longquan Celadon Kilns, thick-glazed stoneware in a soft, jade-like green, from pale plum and sea green to deep leaf green, with a lustrous, unctuous, slightly translucent finish that pools thicker in recesses. Forms are restrained and sculptural, with swelling shoulders and lotus-petal shapes. Decoration is minimal, with carved or moulded petals, incised combed lines and sometimes a fine crackle network. Rims fade lighter where the glaze thins, and the unglazed base burns to russet brown. Quiet, scholarly and understated, like polished river stone.'),
('Ando Cloisonne','East Asia','Meiji-Showa 1880s-1930s','decorative arts','In the style of Ando Cloisonne, smooth, glossy enamel fields held by hair-thin silver or brass wires. Colours are deep and jewel-like, including midnight blue, black, wisteria violet, jade green, ivory and warm gold, with a mirror finish and no visible wire thickness. Subjects are delicate birds, hydrangea, wisteria, irises, chrysanthemums, butterflies and tiny geometric brocade borders, often floating on a plain black or blue ground with generous empty space. Wireless techniques create soft gradients in petals and feathers. Forms are slender, with narrow necks, flared mouths and silver rims.'),
('Kutani Ware','East Asia','Edo-present','ceramics','In the style of Kutani Ware, porcelain painted with dense, opaque overglaze enamels in five dark, saturated colours, namely deep green, Prussian blue, yellow, purple and aubergine red. Designs cover nearly the whole surface with bold landscapes, birds, flowers, geometric diaper patterns and fine black outlines. A second manner uses a bright red ground with gold, carrying tiny figures and ornate panels in minute detail. Green is often laid on thickly as a background with a heavy, jewel-like gloss. Rich, theatrical, almost tapestry-like richness and a thick bright glaze.'),
('Arita Imari Kilns','East Asia','17th-19th century','ceramics','In the style of Arita Imari Kilns, white porcelain decorated in a crowded palette of underglaze cobalt blue, iron red and gold. Panels of chrysanthemums, peonies, pine, bamboo, cranes and phoenix are packed into fan, circle and brocade-pattern reserves that fill every part of the surface. Black outlines, lacy borders, flaring scalloped rims and lobed forms are typical. Red and blue dominate while green and black add accents, and gilding glows on petals and borders. Tall, rounded shapes give an opulent, ornate and festive effect.'),
('Nambu Tekki','East Asia','Edo-present','metalwork', 'In the style of Nambu Tekki, cast-iron design with a heavy, squat, rounded body, a dark matte black or rust-brown finish and a lacquered iron-oxide surface. The skin is covered in rows of raised small round studs, or in smooth walls with fine texture. Details are a flat lid with a small knob in brass or iron, a swinging handle, a firm foot and a thick lip. The surface looks like old weathered metal with a slight sheen, and a few forms carry raised pine, plum or wave motifs. Tea-ceremony restraint, sturdiness and quiet weight.'),
]
